<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 1.3 Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="t00299">
	<title>Checking charging status</title>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01335">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e01336">
								<figgroup>
									<image align="center" href="../../images/N_CT25Q033.eps" scale="95" placement="break"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<fig id="e01337">
								<figgroup>
									<image align="center" href="../../images/N_CT25Q034.eps" scale="95" placement="break"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<ol outputclass="callout" id="e01338">
			<li>
				<p>Charging indicator lamp</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Standby/Unlock</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Start charging/charging</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Scheduled charging</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Charging failure</p>
			</li>
		</ol>
		<p>When charging the high voltage battery, the charge level can be checked from outside the vehicle.</p>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc" pgwide="true" rowsep="1">
			<tgroup cols="3" colsep="1" outputclass="formatc" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colwidth="1*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colwidth="1.24*"/>
				<colspec colname="col3" colnum="3" colwidth="4.57*"/>
				<thead>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry align="center" valign="middle">
							<p>Color</p>
						</entry>
						<entry align="center" valign="middle">
							<p>Time</p>
						</entry>
						<entry align="center" valign="middle">
							<p>Notes</p>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry morerows="1" align="left" valign="middle">
							<p>Sky Blue</p>
						</entry>
						<entry align="center" valign="middle">
							<p>Continuously</p>
						</entry>
						<entry>
							<p>The indicator light turns continuously when the charging door is open or when the vehicle is in standby mode.</p>
						</entry>
					</row>
					<row>
						<entry align="center" valign="middle">
							<p>Blink</p>
						</entry>
						<entry>
							<p>The indicator light blinks when the charging connector is connected, and the vehicle is communicating with the charger.</p>
						</entry>
					</row>
					<row>
						<entry morerows="1" align="left" valign="middle">
							<p>Green</p>
						</entry>
						<entry align="center" valign="middle">
							<p>Continuously</p>
						</entry>
						<entry>
							<p>The indicator light turns continuously when the charge level reaches target charge level.</p>
						</entry>
					</row>
					<row>
						<entry align="center" valign="middle">
							<p>Blink</p>
						</entry>
						<entry>
							<p>The indicator light blinks while charging is in progress.</p>
							<p importance="default">The indicator light blinks more slowly as the vehicle’s charge level increases.</p>
						</entry>
					</row>
					<row>
						<entry colname="col1" align="left" valign="middle">
							<p>Orange</p>
						</entry>
						<entry align="center" valign="middle">
							<p>Continuously</p>
						</entry>
						<entry>
							<p>The indicator light turns continuously when scheduled charging is set.</p>
						</entry>
					</row>
					<row>
						<entry colname="col1" align="left" valign="middle">
							<p>Red</p>
						</entry>
						<entry align="center" valign="middle">
							<p>Blink</p>
						</entry>
						<entry>
							<p>The indicator light blinks if there is an issue preventing charging due to a problem with the vehicle or the charger.</p>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>Charging may not occur under the following circumstances:</p>
		<ul id="e01339">
			<li>
				<p>When the gear is not in P (Park) position.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>If there is an issue with the vehicle’s internal charging system.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>When the internal battery temperature of the vehicle is excessively high.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<ul id="e01340">
			<li>
				<p>If the temperature of the external charger is excessively high or low.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>When the voltage of the external charger is too high or too low.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>If the external charger’s cable is not properly connected.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<note type="note" id="e01341">
			<ul id="e01342">
				<li>
					<p>To prevent driver glare, the brightness of the charging status indicator may be dimmer at night compared to daytime.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</note>
	</conbody>
</concept>